{"name":"Overgrown Temple","hex":"#116611","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"overgrown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having large numbers of plants which have become too big, and are hence spoiling the picturesqueness of a garden.","Having grown bigger without developing maturity or changing character."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["past participle of overgrow"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overgrown"},{"term":"temple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A house of worship, especially:\nA house of worship dedicated to a polytheistic faith.","A house of worship dedicated to a polytheistic faith."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To build a temple for; to appropriate a temple to; to temple a god"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/temple"}],"entries":[{"title":"Overgrown","blocks":[{"text":"Overgrown is the second studio album by English singer-songwriter James Blake. It was released on 5 April 2013 by Blake's Atlas Records, along with Republic Records and Polydor Records. The album features guest appearances from Wu-Tang Clan member RZA and English musician Brian Eno. Overgrown debuted at number eight on the UK Albums Chart and at number one on the US Dance/Electronic chart. It was supported by lead single \"Retrograde\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/de/James_Blake_-_Overgrown_album_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Overgrown","wikidata":"Q7113670"},{"title":"Temple","blocks":[{"text":"A temple is a place of worship, a building used for spiritual rituals and activities such as prayer and sacrifice. By convention, the specially built places of worship for some religions are commonly called \"temples\" in English, while those of other religions are not, even though they fulfill very similar functions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thu